==Background==
===Development===
[[File:BB21 Logo.jpg|250px|thumb|right|Promotional Logo]]
CBS announced that ''Big Brother'' had been renewed for a twenty-first and twenty-second season on May 15, 2019. CBS later announced on May 20, that the twenty-first season was set to premiere on June 25, 2019.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://tvline.com/2019/05/20/big-brother-season-21-premiere-date/|title=Big Brother Season 21 Premiere Date Set, Status of Celebrity Editions TBD|last=Webb Mitovich|first=Matt|date=May 20, 2019|accessdate=May 20, 2019|work=TV Line}}</ref> Unnamed insiders close to the production of the show previously cast doubt if [[Julie Chen-Moonves|Julie Chen]] would return to host following sexual misconduct allegations against her husband Les Moonves.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://people.com/tv/big-brother-staff-nervous-julie-chen-will-leave/ |title=Big Brother Staff Is ‘Nervous’ Julie Chen Will Leave amid Husband Les Moonves’ Scandal: Source |last=Helling |first=Steve |last2=Dugan |first2=Christina |date=September 19, 2018 |website=PEOPLE.com |language=en |access-date=September 19, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180919053545/https://people.com/tv/big-brother-staff-nervous-julie-chen-will-leave/ |archive-date=2018-09-19 |dead-url=no |df= }}</ref> Chen Moonves however, returned for ''[[Celebrity Big Brother 2 (US)]]'' and it was later announced that Julie Chen Moonves would return to season 21.<ref name="The Futon Critic">{{cite web|url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/news/2019/05/20/perennial-summer-favorite-big-brother-returns-with-a-two-night-premiere-event-tuesday-june-25-and-wednesday-june-26-800-900-pm-906010/20190520cbs01/|title=Perennial Summer Favorite "Big Brother" Returns with a Two-Night Premiere Event Tuesday, June 25 and Wednesday, June 26, 8:00-9:00 PM|date=May 20, 2019|accessdate=May 20, 2019|work=The Futon Critic}}</ref>

Allison Grodner and Rich Meehan to return as executive producers for the series which is produced by Fly on the Wall Entertainment, in association with Endemol Shine North America.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://cbspressexpress.com/cbs-entertainment/shows/big-brother/releases/view?id=52703|title=PERENNIAL SUMMER FAVORITE “BIG BROTHER” RETURNS WITH A TWO-NIGHT PREMIERE EVENT TUESDAY, JUNE 25 AND WEDNESDAY, JUNE 26, 8:00-9:00 PM|date=May 20, 2019|accessdate=June 10, 2019|work=CBS Press Express}}</ref>
===Casting===
Despite not having an official renewal announcement from CBS at the time, casting for the season was open until April 2019.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bigbrothercasting.tv/home|title=Big Brother Casting|accessdate=June 10, 2019|work=Big Brother Casting}}</ref> Kassting, Inc. returned to provide casting services for a twentieth consecutive season since [[Big Brother 2 (US)|season 2]] with Robyn Kass serving as the casting director.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://kasstinginc.com/showlist.php|title=Kassting, Inc. - Showlist|accessdate=June 10, 2019|work=Kassting, Inc.}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://kasstinginc.com/company-info.php|title=Kasting, Inc. - Company Info|accessdate=June 10, 2019|work=Kassting, Inc.}}</ref>

It was then announced by former [[Big Brother 11 (US)|season 11]] & [[Big Brother 13 (US)|season 13]] contestant, [[Jeff Schroeder]] that the houseguests would officially be introduced on June 17 at 11 AM ET/8 AM PT on the live feeds, after they were released an hour earlier.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/CBSBigBrother/status/1138131086599344131|last=CBSBigBrother|date=10 June 2019|accessdate=17 June 2019|title=He's back! Meet the new Houseguests in ONE week with @jeffschroeder23. ☀️ #BB21|work=Twitter}}</ref>
====Cast Relationships====
Moments after the cast was revealed, it was noticed by fans that many of the new houseguests have a relationship with one another. [[Christie Murphy]] used to date [[Tommy Bracco|Tommy Bracco's]] aunt and is tagged in many of each other's Instagram photos.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/hamsterwatch/status/1140661462500696068|last=hamsterwatch|date=17 June 2019|accessdate=20 June 2019|title=a little birdie has told me that Christie and Tommy know each other #bb21|work=Twitter}}</ref> It was revealed by [https://robhasawebsite.com/ Rob Has a Podcast] Live Feed Correspondent, [https://twitter.com/OneLuckyGay Brent Wolgamott] that [[Holly Allen]] and [[Kathryn Dunn]] were friends and knew that they would be cast together for weeks prior to sequester.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/OneLuckyGay/status/1140673523284938753|first=Brent|last=Wolgamott|date=17 June 2019|accessdate=20 June 2019|title=Nope. Holly and Kat know each other. Somethin’ goin on? Also, them’s the two cast members I knew 2 weeks ago.|work=Twitter}}</ref>

===Air Schedule===
The season features an initial time slot change from previous seasons; new episodes are set to air on a Sunday/Tuesday/Wednesday schedule through the first six episodes before returning to a traditional Sunday/Wednesday/Thursday schedule as in previous seasons.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://bigbrothernetwork.com/big-brother-21-schedule-dates-times/|title=Big Brother 21 Schedule & Start Date|last=Boyer|first=Matt|date=May 20, 2019|accessdate=May 23, 2019|work=Big Brother Network}}</ref>

The 24/7 internet live feeds are also expected to return with a CBS All Access subscription following the two-night season premiere on June 26.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://bigbrothernetwork.com/big-brother-21-houseguests-reveal-planned/|title=Big Brother 21 Houseguests’ Reveal Announcement News|last=Boyer|first=Matt|date=June 10, 2019|accessdate=June 10, 2019|work=Big Brother Network}}</ref> In addition, ''[[Big Brother: After Dark]]'' is expected to return on Pop also following the two-night premiere on June 26 or June 27, depending on viewers local time zones.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.tvguide.com/listings/|title=TV Listings|accessdate=June 12, 2019|work=TV Guide}}</ref>
===House Reveal===
As with previous seasons, the program is filmed at CBS Studios, sound stage 18 in a custom-built two story house.<ref name="House-1">{{Cite web |url=https://variety.com/2005/scene/markets-festivals/cbs-ramps-up-summer-reality-sked-1117922274/ |title=CBS ramps up summer reality sked |last=Adalian |first=Josef |date=May 6, 2005 |website=Variety |language=en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181025150117/https://variety.com/2005/scene/markets-festivals/cbs-ramps-up-summer-reality-sked-1117922274/ |archive-date=25 October 25 2018 |dead-url=no |access-date=18 January 2019}}</ref><ref name="House-CBS">{{Cite web |url=https://www.cbs.com/shows/big_brother/news/1007499/here-s-what-it-s-like-to-attend-a-big-brother-live-eviction-show/ |title=Here's What It's Like To Attend A Big Brother Live Eviction Show  |date=29 August 2017 |website=CBS.com |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180101145934/https://www.cbs.com/shows/big_brother/news/1007499/here-s-what-it-s-like-to-attend-a-big-brother-live-eviction-show/ |archive-date=1 January 2018 |dead-url=no |access-date=18 January 2019}}</ref> The House is equipped with 94 high-definition cameras and over 113 microphones in order to monitor and record the houseguests.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://cbspressexpress.com/cbs-entertainment/shows/big-brother/about|title=BIG BROTHER|date=June 2019|accessdate=June 21, 2019|work=CBS Press Express}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://cbspressexpress.com/cbs-entertainment/shows/big-brother/releases/view?id=52924|title=CBS ANNOUNCES 16 NEW HOUSEGUESTS FOR “BIG BROTHER’S” 21st SEASON!|date=17 June 2019|accessdate=21 June 2019|work=CBS Press Express}}</ref> The living room, three bedrooms, kitchen, dining room, bathroom, and lounge room are located on the first floor.<ref name="House photos">{{cite web|url=https://bigbrothernetwork.com/big-brother-21-house-tour/|title=Big Brother 21 House Tour: Photos & Video|last=Boyer|first=Matt|date=21 June 2019|accessdate=21 June 2019|work=Big Brother Network}}</ref> The [[Head of Household]] bedroom and bathroom, and an additional lounge area known as the "Sky Bridge" are located on the second floor.<ref name="House photos" /> The second floor is accessible by a ladder located in the entry way or a spiral staircase located in the kitchen next to the sliding glass doors that lead to the backyard.<ref name="House photos" /> The backyard area features outdoor amenities for the houseguests.<ref name="House photos" /> ''[[wikipedia:Entertainment Tonight|Entertainment Tonight]]'' showed the first look at the house with [[wikipedia:Kevin Frazier|Kevin Frazier]] during their episode on the night of June 20, 2019.<ref>{{cite web |title="Entertainment Tonight" Episode #38.244 |url=https://www.imdb.com/title/tt10492848/ |website=IMDb |accessdate=22 June 2019}}</ref> ''Entertainment Tonight'' then released a sneak peek of the house through a brief tour on their website on June 21.<ref name="ET House & 99 Days">{{cite web|url=https://www.etonline.com/big-brother-season-21-tour-the-camp-themed-house-exclusive-127437|title='Big Brother' Season 21: Tour the Camp-Themed House! (Exclusive)|last=Seemayer|first=Zach|date=21 June 2019|accessdate=21 June 2019|work=Entertainment Weekly}}</ref> Meanwhile, a full house tour with the host, [[Julie Chen-Moonves|Julie Chen]], and other photos were released through the show's social media outlets.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.instagram.com/tv/By-ePutgeCW/|title=Summer camp is in session! 🏕 @juliechencbs provides a sneak peek at the #BB21 house inspired by the great outdoors. Two-night premiere event 6/25 and 6/26 8-9pmET/PT on #CBS.|date=21 June 2019|accessdate=21 June 2019|work=IGTV}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.instagram.com/p/By-ytrOp979/|title=Swipe to take a closer look at the “summer camp-themed” #BB21 house! ➡️🏕🦉|date=21 June 2019|accessdate=21 June 2019|work=Instagram}}</ref><ref>{{cite tweet|number=1142084761470423040|title=The #BB21 doors have swung open. Step right in... 🚪|date=21 June 2019|accessdate=21 June 2019|user=CBSBigBrother}}</ref><ref>{{cite tweet|number=1142130006803410949|title=Camp is in session as this summer’s #BB21 house is REVEALED! ⛺️🔥🎣 This season's "summer camp-themed living" brings the great outdoors in. Check out these four spaces in the new house!|date=21 June 2019|accessdate=21 June 2019|user=CBSBigBrother}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.facebook.com/BigBrother/videos/2422288984500493/|title=The BB21 doors have swung open. Step right in... 🚪|date=21 June 2019|accessdate=21 June 2019|work=Facebook}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.facebook.com/BigBrother/posts/10156938883624473|title=Camp is in session as this summer’s BB21 house is REVEALED! ⛺️🔥🎣 This season's "summer camp-themed living" brings the great outdoors in. Check out every corner of the new house!|date=21 June|accessdate=21 June 2019|work=Facebook}}</ref>

The house theme matched the season's overall theme and received a camp theme; Production Designer Scott Storey designed the house's features.<ref name="House overall">{{cite web|url=https://cbspressexpress.com/cbs-entertainment/shows/big-brother/releases/view?id=52971|title=“BIG BROTHER” SEASON 21 HOUSE THEME REVEALED|date=21 June 2019|accessdate=21 June 2019|work=CBS Press Express}}</ref> The living room features a birch-wood coffee table and a large and a 23-foot triangular window illuminated by LED lights.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.tvguide.com/news/big-brother-21-house-theme-camp/|title=The Big Brother 21 House Is Taking the Players to Summer Camp|last=Gennis|first=Sadie|date=21 June 2019|accessdate=21 June 2019|work=TV Guide}}</ref> The first bedroom features a "sleeping under the stars" theme and includes two double-beds and the exterior of a camper.<ref name="Bedrooms">{{cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZBLwNukQAnU|title=See Julie Chen Show Off New "Big Brother" House (Exclusive)|author=E! News|work=YouTube|date=21 June 2019|accessdate=21 June 2019}}</ref> The camper, is only a facade into the second bedroom which features three double-beds and is assumed to be that of a camp counselor's bedroom.<ref name="Bedrooms" /> The third and final downstairs bedroom is a sports-themed bedroom primarily based from archery.<ref name="Bedrooms" /> In the kitchen many of the appliances have been redone in an attempted to blend them in with the rest of the theme, an electronic camp fire has been added to the center of formal dining table.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.newsweek.com/big-brother-house-reveal-season-21-1445062|title='BIG BROTHER' HOUSE REVEAL: EXCLUSIVE VIDEO OF CAMP-THEMED LIVING ROOM, KITCHEN AND DINING ROOM|last=Wynne|first=Kelly|date=21 June 2019|accessdate=21 June 2019|work=Newsweek}}</ref> The downstairs lounge area received a boat theme while the bathroom received a boat house like theme.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://ew.com/tv/2019/06/21/big-brother-21-new-house-tour-video/|title=Get an exclusive first look at the new Big Brother house|last=Ross|first=Dalton|date=21 June 2019|accessdate=21 June 2019|work=Entertainment Weekly}}</ref> The upstairs lounge area, for the first time in the series history is also accessible by a ladder from the entry way, has been updated to resemble a tree house; the Head of Household bedroom and bathroom have been changed to resemble a Moroccan-style bedroom.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://cbspressexpress.com/cbs-entertainment/shows/big-brother/video|title=Big Brother 21 House Tour|date=21 June 2019|accessdate=21 June 2019|work=CBS Press Express}}</ref> The backyard features a pool with kayak's and an attached hot tub, lawn chairs surround the back yard which also features a pool table and a washer and dryer, workout equipment, outdoor lounge areas, a hammock, and a mini-fridge.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.usmagazine.com/entertainment/pictures/big-brother-season-21-theme-house-revealed-photos/|title=‘Big Brother’ Season 21 Theme and House Revealed: Inside Photos|last=Longretta|first=Emily|date=21 June 2019|accessdate=21 June 2019|work=US Weekly}}</ref>
