===Premiere Night Alleged Racism===
[[File:BB21 Jackson Camp Director.png|250px|thumb|right]]
Following the two-night season premiere viewers accused houseguest [[Jackson Michie]] of discriminating against race and age.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.oprahmag.com/entertainment/tv-movies/a28206876/big-brother-season-21-racism-twitter-reactions/|title=Big Brother Fans Are Saying There's Already Racism and Ageism Inside the House|last=Dibdin|first=Emma|date=27 June 2019|accessdate=1 July 2019|work=Oprah Magazine}}</ref>Jackson received the [[Camp Director]] power and was required to choose four houseguests to banish.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.yahoo.com/entertainment/big-brother-just-premiered-and-twitter-is-already-calling-out-its-racism-032657145.html|title='Big Brother' just premiered and Twitter is already calling out its racism|last=Mar|first=Kylie|date=26 June 2019|accessdate=1 July 2019|work=Yahoo! Entertainment}}</ref> Jackson chose to banish included the seasons only two African American contestants, the Hispanic-American plus size model, along with the oldest person in the house.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.cheatsheet.com/entertainment/big-brother-21-is-this-houseguest-racist-fans-think-so.html/|title='Big Brother 21': Is This Houseguest Racist? Fans Think So|last=Montford|first=Christina|date=27 June 2019|accessdate=1 July 2019|work=CheatSheet}}</ref> Viewers then questioned the series for the [[Head of Household]] competition which occurred the same night and was named "Color War."<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.newsweek.com/big-brother-21-racist-elimination-twitter-1446278|title='BIG BROTHER' 21 IS ALREADY BEING CALLED RACIST TWO NIGHTS INTO THE NEW SEASON: HERE'S WHY|last=Wynne|first=Kelly|date=27 June 2019|accessdate=1 July 2019|work=Newsweek}}</ref>
===Jack Matthews' Comments===
[[File:BB21 Jack Warned.jpg|250px|thumb|right]]
Once the 24/7 live feeds began some viewers began calling for CBS to remove HouseGuest Jack Matthews from the series.<ref name="Matthews petition">{{cite web|url=https://www.cheatsheet.com/entertainment/big-brother-21-fans-create-a-petition-to-get-jack-matthews-ejected-from-the-house.html/|title='Big Brother 21' Fans Create a Petition to Get Jack Matthews Ejected from the House|last=Weaver|first=Nicole|date=1 July 2019|accessdate=2 July 2019|work=CheatSheet}}</ref> Matthews was seen on the live feeds making vicious and violent remarks about [[Kemi Fakunle]], behind her back.<ref name="Matthews petition 2">{{cite web|url=https://www.oprahmag.com/entertainment/tv-movies/a28244210/big-brother-21-jack-matthews-change-org-petition-expelled/|title=Big Brother 21: The Reason Fans Are Petitioning to Kick Jack Matthews Off the Show|last=Jean-Philippe|first=McKenzie|date=1 July 2019|accessdate=2 July 2019|work=Oprah Magazine}}</ref> About Fakunle, Matthews said that she is "fucking poison"; ahead of the Power of Veto competition he stated "B*tch, you're fucking going up and you can play your f*ckin' veto, but I'm gonna f*ck you up!"<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.yahoo.com/lifestyle/big-brother-fans-petitioning-player-170000661.html|title=Big Brother Fans Are Petitioning to Get This Player Expelled From the Show|last=Jean-Philippe|first=McKenzie|date=1 July 2019|accessdate=2 July= 2019|work=Yahoo! Lifestyle}}</ref> Most notably Matthews stated "F*cking Kemi makes me want to f*cking stomp a mud hole right through her chest."<ref name="Matthews petition 2" /> Aside from this Matthews was also seen making other derogatory comments against other contestants including [[Ovi Kabir]] who he called a "brown flame" and [[Jessica Milagros]] who he called a "maggot."<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.knoxnews.com/story/entertainment/columnists/chuck-campbell/2019/07/02/big-brother-fans-want-jack-matthews-booted-derogatory-comments/1624251001/|title='Big Brother': Fans want Jack booted for derogatory comments about Kemi, Knoxville's Ovi|last=Campbell|first=Chuck|date=2 July 2019|accessdate=2 July 2019|work=Knox News}}</ref> A Change.org petition was started in an attempt to get Matthews removed from the game for Fakunle's and others safety.<ref name="Matthews petition" /> Matthews was warned by production about comments made and to prevent further such comments.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://bigbrothernetwork.com/big-brother-21-jack-warned-by-production-about-comments-made/|title=Big Brother 21: Jack Warned by Production About Comments Made|last=Slogeris|first=Tammie|date=2 July 2019|accessdate=2 July 2019|work=Big Brother Network}}</ref> Meanwhile other live feed viewers state that the CBS disclaimer has appeared more since the incident.<ref name="CBS disclaimer">{{cite web|url=https://www.realityblurred.com/realitytv/2019/07/bb21-jack-jackson-kemi-warning/|title=Big Brother’s Jack warned by producers after houseguests’ toxic comments increased|last=Dehnart|first=Andy|date=1 July 2019|accessdate=2 July 2019|work=Reality Blurred}}</ref>

Weeks later during Week 4, Jack would make additional comments about Asian-American houseguest [[Isabella Wang]]. He was in a hammock with the members of the [[Six Shooters]] alliance, he then proceeded to make a joke about rice pudding. At that point, that would have been the second time he made a "rice pudding" joke that week.<ref name="Rice Pudding TMZ">{{cite web|url=https://www.tmz.com/2019/07/24/big-brother-rice-pudding-joke-asian-jack-matthews-isabella-wang-racism/|title='Big Brother' Houseguest Cracks 'Rice Pudding' Joke About Asian Houseguest|date=24 July 2019|accessdate=24 July 2019|work=TMZ}}</ref>

Following Matthews' eviction Week 6, host Julie Chen-Moonves asked him about his comments, in which Matthews denied all allegations of racism.

===Treatment of David Alexander===
[[File:Big-brother-jack-matthews-jackson-michie-1.jpg|thumb|right|250px]]

[[File:Jackson Kat Mexico.png|thumb|right|250px]]
Just earlier, Jackson alongside [[Kathryn Dunn]] were talking about David in the Head of Household room where he stated that David should “Go back to Mexico" <ref name="David Treatment 3">{{cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vpmZbJ2jQw8|title=BB21 FULL CONVERSATION "Go back to Mexico"|last=gabby|date=4 July 2019|accessdate=5 July 2019|work=YouTube}}</ref>after Kathryn called him a snake. He would later on state that he would like to “mule kick him [David] in the teeth." He would go on to receiving a warning from the Diary Room, which led him to concerning about how it was being perceived in the outside world.<ref name="David Treatment 2">{{cite web|url=https://soapdirt.com/big-brother-21-jackson-michie-and-jack-drop-the-n-word-about-david/|title=‘Big Brother 21’: Jackson Michie and Jack Drop the ‘N-Word’ About David?|last=Clark|first=Rachel|date=5 July 2019|accessdate=5 July 2019|work=Soap Dirt}}</ref>
===Treatment of Nicole Anthony===
[[File:Grateful HOH.jpg|250px|thumb|right]]
There has also been a significant amount of backlash towards HouseGuest [[Isabella Wang]] and the [[Gr8ful]] alliance for bullying fellow HouseGuest [[Nicole Anthony]], which was shown during Episode 10.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://popculture.com/reality-tv/2019/07/18/big-brother-fans-trash-isabella-wang-gr8ful-alliance-after-meltdowns-bunch-mean-kids/|last=Bastidas|first=Jose|date=17 July 2019|accessdate=19 July 2019|work=Popculture.com}}</ref> Wang has been accused of targeting and bullying Anthony because of things that she told Wang about their alliance wanting to nominate her and fellow HouseGuest [[Nick Maccarone]] for eviction, which the alliance falsely denied. Multiple fans of the show have condemned this behavior and dubbed the Gr8ful alliance the "H8ful" alliance which the narrator of the show alluded to during the episode.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://bigbrothernetwork.com/big-brother-21-episode-10-recap-gr8ful-gets-hateful/|title=Big Brother 21 Episode 10 Recap: Gr8ful Gets Hateful|first=Branden|date=17 July 2019|accessdate=19 July 2019|work=Big Brother Network}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://theinterrobang.com/big-brothers-bb21-epsiode-2-the-hateful-gr8ful/|last=Calise|first=Vito|date=5 July 2019|accessdate=19 July 2019|work=The Interro Bang}}</ref>
===Jackson As Have-Not===
[[File:Jackson HN Shower.png|250px|thumb|right]]
At the beginning of week four Cliff Hogg, as the [[Head of Household]], was required to name four houseguests to become have-nots for the week.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.inquisitr.com/5539564/big-brother-21-first-four-have-nots-of-the-season-revealed/|title=‘Big Brother’ 21: First Four Have-Nots Of The Season Revealed|last=Albers|first=Caitlin|date=19 July 2019|accessdate=15 August 2019|work=Inquisitr}}</ref> Have-nots are required to take cold showers, eat only slop, and sleep in less than ideal beds during the week.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://popculture.com/reality-tv/2019/08/02/big-brother-huge-argument-ensues-before-sam-smith-eviction-fans-wonder-what-just-happened/|title='Big Brother' Fans Want Jack Matthews Gone Despite Surprising Veto Outcome|last=Bastidas|first=Jose|date=July 24, 2019|accessdate=August 5, 2019|work=Popculture}}</ref> Along with three others Hogg named Jackson Michie to become a have-not.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.cbs.com/shows/big_brother/news/1009328/big-brother-21-episode-recaps--another-houseguest-leaves-the-game/|title=Big Brother 21 Episode Recaps: Another Houseguest Leaves The Game|date=2 August 2019|accessdate=15 August 2019|work=CBS}}</ref> Despite being named as a have-not Michie was seen on the 24/7 live feeds breaking the have-not rules by stuffing his pockets full of food and eating it behind the shower wall out of camera view.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://ew.com/tv/2019/07/31/michie-big-brother-live-feeds-surprising-facts/|title=3 things about Michie Big Brother fans are missing if they aren’t watching the live feeds|last=Tew|first=Caroline|date=31 July 2019|accessdate=15 August 2019|work=Entertainment Weekly}}</ref> Michie received no punishment normally given to houseguests who break the have-not rules.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.cinemablend.com/television/2477282/5-ways-cbs-can-fix-big-brother-after-2019-mess|title=5 Ways CBS Can Fix Big Brother After 2019 Mess|last=Carbone|first=Gina|date=1 August 2019|accessdate=15 August 2019|work=Cinema Blend}}</ref> In past seasons of ''Big Brother'' houseguests have received eviction votes or other penalties for breaking the have-not rules.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.realityblurred.com/realitytv/2007/08/big-brother-8-jen_evicted/|title=Jen evicted after receiving Big Brother’s first-ever penalty vote|last=Dehnart|first=Andy|date=24 August 2007|accessdate15 August 2019|work=Reality Blurred}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.hamsterwatch.com/bb11/080509.shtml|title=Day 32 - August 5, 2009|date=5 August 2009|accessdate=15 August 2019}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://bigbrothernetwork.com/big-brother-19-matthew-clines-penalty-vote/|title=‘Big Brother 19’ Live Feeds: Matthew Clines Receives Penalty Vote [POLL]|last=Boyer|first=Matt|date=29 August 2017|accessdate=15 August 2019|work=Big Brother Network}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.monstersandcritics.com/smallscreen/will-big-brother-punish-jackson-michie-for-sneaking-food-as-a-have-not/|title=Will Big Brother punish Jackson Michie for sneaking food as a Have-Not?|last=DeVault|first=Ryan|date=22 July 2019|accessdate=15 August 2019|work=Monsters and Critics}}</ref> Viewers of the series took to social media calling for ''Big Brother'' to enforce rules as done in the past by punishing Michie and not give special treatment.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.inquisitr.com/5549004/big-brother-21-jackson-michie-caught-cheating-several-times-while-on-slop/|title=‘Big Brother 21:’ Jackson Michie Caught Cheating Several Times While On Slop|last=Albers|first=Caitlin|date=25 July 2019|accessdate=15 August 2019|work=Inquisitr}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.cheatsheet.com/entertainment/big-brother-21-fans-think-this-houseguest-is-cheating-while-on-slop-and-are-calling-for-punishment.html/|title='Big Brother 21' Fans Think This Houseguest Is Cheating While on Slop and Are Calling for Punishment|last=Weaver|first=Nicole|date=24 July 2019|accessdate=15 August 2019|work=Showbiz CheatSheet}}</ref> After the end of week five, the have-not phase ended for the season, likely in response to the controversy surrounding Jackson, and an attempt to prevent any repeat violations. It is worth noting however, Jackson alluded to possibly having an eating disorder and that production was not made aware of that before he was cast.

===Producer Reprimanded===
[[File:2CvPN7V .jpg|250px|thumb|right]]
At the 2019 Television Critics Association CBS executives were questioned about diversity and racism issues on ''Big Brother'' as well as fellow CBS television series .<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.thewrap.com/cbs-execs-respond-to-racism-big-brother-fiery-tca-session/|title=CBS Execs Respond to ‘Big Brother’ Racism Accusations During Fiery Press Session|last=Sippell|first=Margeaux|date=1 August 2019|accessdate=14 August 2019|work=The Wrap}}</ref> In an open interview with CBS executives, ''Big Brother'' was accused of giving "contestants of color unfair cuts or early eliminations" as well as editing out comments by contestants that have been interpreted as racist.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://decider.com/2019/08/01/cbs-big-brother-survivor-racism-accusations/|title=CBS Addresses ‘Survivor,’ ‘Big Brother’ Racism Accusations|last=Cobb|first=Kayla|date=1 August 2019|accessdate=14 August 2019|work=Decider}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/live-feed/cbs-execs-address-issues-bull-big-brother-1228555|title=CBS Brass Grilled on Representation on Reality Shows, 'Bull' Renewal|last=O'Connell|first=Michael|date=1 August 2019|accessdate=14 August 20199|work=The Hollywood Reporter}}</ref> CBS executives defended editors of the show stating that it's difficult to edit days worth of content into forty-minutes.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.oregonlive.com/entertainment/2019/08/cbs-executives-pressed-about-bull-and-big-brother-controversies-over-sexual-harassment-and-racism-tv-press-tour.html|title=CBS executives pressed on ‘Bull’ and ‘Big Brother’ controversies over sexual harassment and racism: TV press tour|last=Turnquist|first=Krist|date=1 August 2019|accessdate=14 August 2019|work=Oregon Live}}</ref> Speaking on a similar but separate incident one press member specifically asked about situation of Kemi Fakunle, who after being evicted claimed series producers tried to goad her into playing the part of a "sassy black woman."<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2019/08/big-brother-survivor-diversity-problems-cbs-exectutives-comment-tca-1202658702/|title=CBS Brass Face Criticism Over Diversity Issues On ‘Big Brother’, ‘Survivor’ – TCA|last=D'Alessandro|first=Anthony|date=1 August 2019|accessdate=14 August 2019|work=Deadline Hollywood}}</ref> It was later revealed by the Big Brother Wiki that it was Supervising Producer Christine Owen, after reports of Kemi stating that the producer she referred to as Christine.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://twitter.com/bigbrotherwikia/status/1156993742844379137|title=Big Brother 21 Supervising Producer, Christine Owen, reprimanded after trying to portray Kemi in a stereotypical limelight #BB21|last=Big Brother Wikia|date=1 August 2019|accessdate=14 August 2019|work=Twitter}}</ref>
[[File:Thom-sherman-kelly-kahl-cbs-tca-summer-2019.jpg|250px|thumb|right]]
CBS Executive Tom Sherman stated, "Well, in the case of Big Brother, a producer—we learned that a producer, in an attempt to get a soundbite from one of the houseguests overstepped. That producer was reprimanded, received unconscious bias training—as did all the producers on the show—and we don’t believe that an incident like that will happen again."|<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.realityblurred.com/realitytv/2019/08/cbs-executives-survivor-big-brother-racism-diversity-inclusion/|title=CBS executives on Survivor and Big Brother’s diversity, inclusion, and racism|last=Dehnart|first=Andy|date=1 August 2019|accessdate=14 August 2019|work=Reality Blurred}}</ref>

The CBS executives in question responded by stating that they investigated the situation, found the producer in question overstepped, reprimanded the said producer, and as a result trained all of their producers.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/tv/2019/08/01/pauley-perrette-cbs-responds-harassment-charges/1890488001/|title=CBS responds to Pauley Perrette's accusations, 'Big Brother' racism|last=Levin|first=Gary|date=1 August 2019|accessdate=14 August 2019|work=USA Today}}</ref> Finally, CBS executives also stated that they would "closely reexamine ''Big Brother 21'' and see if we can do better next year."<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.goldderby.com/article/2019/big-brother-21-racism-comments-edits-cbs-responds/|title=CBS bosses will reexamine ‘Big Brother 21’ and see if ‘we can do better next year’ in the wake of racism controversy|last=Eng|first=Joyce|date=1 August 2019|accessdate=14 August 2019|work=GoldDerby}}</ref>

===PETA Week 5 Sheep Cruelty===
[[File:Cliff-During-BB21-POV.jpg|250px|thumb|right]]
The use of animals in the week five Power of Veto competition sparked criticism from viewers and national organizations accusing CBS and ''Big Brother'' of animal cruelty.<ref name="Oprah Mag animal cruelty">{{cite web|url=https://www.oprahmag.com/entertainment/tv-movies/a28578498/big-brother-season-21-episode-16-spoilers-veto-competition/|title=Big Brother Fans Are Furious That Houseguests Were Tasked with Herding Live Sheep|last=Borge|first=Jonathan|date=1 August 2019|accessdate=2 August 2019|work=Oprah Magazine}}</ref> In the competitions sheep had been dressed with random numbers and competing HouseGuests were required to wrangle sheep into enclosed pins to add up to a pre-defined given number.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.cheatsheet.com/entertainment/big-brother-21-why-the-shows-latest-veto-competition-is-upsetting-alums-and-fans.html/|title='Big Brother 21': Why the Show's Latest Veto Competition Is Upsetting Alums and Fans|last=Weaver|first=Nicole|date=1 August  2018|accessdate=2 August 2019|work=Showbiz CheatSheet}}</ref> PETA, also known as the People for the Ethical Treatment of Animals, spoke out against CBS and ''Big Brother'' on social media stating that "Animals are not entertainment," "Animals are not yours to abuse," and calling for them to commit to not using live animals again.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.facebook.com/official.peta/photos/a.55746449585/10157733227904586/?type=3&theater|title=ATTENTION Big Brother & CBS: Sheep are timid, gentle animals — forcing them to try escaping from #BB21 contestants chasing & grabbing at them is cruelty to animals. Commit to NEVER having live animals on your show again!|date=August 1, 2019|accessdate=August 2, 2019|author=PETA|work=Facebook}}</ref><ref name="PETA tweet">{{cite tweet|number=1157008611765174272|title=ATTN @CBS: Animals are NOT yours to abuse! On last night’s episode of @CBSBigBrother, contestants chased terrified sheep for a foolish competition. Commit to never having live animals on screen again! #BB21|date=August 1, 2019|accessdate=August 2, 2019|author=PETA|author-link=People for the Ethical Treatment of Animals|user=peta}}</ref> Additionally, viewers also took to social media calling for similar requests and speaking out against the show's current and past use of animals as well, most notably the use of snakes and cockroaches in other competitions earlier in the season.<ref name="Oprah Mag animal cruelty"/>
===Julie Chen Gypsy Slur===
[[File:EBgg5vEU4AAvZGO-660x383.jpg|250px|thumb|right]]
During Jack Matthews' eviction interview, aired on episode 20, host Julie Chen Moonves said a racial slur in saying, “We didn’t gyp you out of goodbye videos.” The word ''gyp'' and ''gypped'' are considered racial slurs to Gypsies.<ref>{{cite web|title=Judge accused of using racial slur against gypsies|url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/uknews/law-and-order/5483053/Judge-accused-of-using-racial-slur-against-gypsies.html|website=The Telegraph|accessdate=14 August 2019}}</ref> Some fans of the show commented on the situational irony when Chen Moonves was interviewing Matthews on many derogatory actions he made, but then proceeded to make a racial slur. However, many fans did not know it was a racial slur until complaints were made on social media.<ref>{{cite web|last1=Tinoco|first1=Armando|title='Big Brother 21': Why Fans Are Calling Julie Chen Out For This Racial Slur|url=https://www.cheatsheet.com/entertainment/big-brother-21-julie-chen-racial-slur-cbs.html/|website=Showbiz CheatSheet|accessdate=14 August 2019}}</ref>
===Finale Night Callouts===
On the live finale night, while the Final Two were being questioned by the Jury, Juror [[Tommy Bracco]] called out eventual winner [[Jackson Michie]] for being sexist and treating women harshly. During the Jury Roundtable hosted by ''[[Big Brother 2 (US)]]'' winner [[Will Kirby]], Tommy had also mentioned that Jackson had specifically been degrading towards [[Kathryn Dunn]] and [[Christie Murphy]].

After the votes had been cast, host Julie Chen Moonves opened up the floor for the pre-jurors, specifically [[Ovi Kabir]], [[Kemi Fakunle]], [[David Alexander]] and [[Isabella Wang]] to speak on all of the controversy that had struck. Ovi had called out the aforementioned bullying of [[Nicole Anthony]] done on by the [[Gr8ful]]/[[Unde9able]] alliance. Kemi called out Christie, [[Nick Maccarone]], [[Jack Matthews]], and Jackson on their obsession and constant bashing towards her, even after her eviction. After being led into by Julie, David had spoken on Jackson's actions on Day 1 as the Camp Director. And Isabella was able to confront Nick for cheating on her with Kathryn while they were in [[The Jury|the Jury House]] and "making her look stupid", something that he promised her he would not do.

After Jackson had been crowned the winner in a vote of 6-3, his reaction was not as exciting as one would expect, with fans dubbing it "the most somber winner reveal in ''Big Brother'' history", with some suggesting that he could not truly enjoy his victory due to being called sexist and racist just moments prior to winning.

==Trivia==
[[File:BB21 Memory Wall.jpg|250px|thumb|right|The Season 21 Memory Wall.]]
*With their 21st season, the ''[[Big Brother U.S. (franchise)|Big Brother U.S.]]'' English speaking edition will be the first country to air 21 civilian seasons of the show.
*This is the first season since [[Big Brother 17 (US)|Big Brother 17]] in which the eventual winner did not win by a 5-4 vote.
**[[Jackson Michie]] won by a 6-3 vote.
*This season is tied with [[Big Brother 14 (US)|Big Brother 14]] and [[Big Brother 22 (US)|Big Brother 22]] for the most amount of consecutive HoHs to also win the PoV with three.
**This was accomplished by [[Jessica Milagros|Jessica]], [[Tommy Bracco|Tommy]], and [[Jackson Michie|Jackson]] during weeks 6, 7, and 8 respectively.
*This is the first odd-numbered season not to feature a tie-breaking vote since ''[[Big Brother 7 (US)|Big Brother 7]]''.
*This season has the shortest [[Have-Not]] Phase, with it only lasting for two weeks.
*The opening sequence included the theme music last used from ''[[Big Brother 11 (US)]]'' to ''[[Big Brother 13 (US)]]''.
*Coincidentally, the first and last evictee both returned for ''[[Big Brother 22 (US)|Big Brother 22]]''.
*This is the first season since [[Big Brother 13 (US)|Big Brother 13]] where only one Houseguest ([[Jackson Michie|Jackson]]) won 5 or more competitions.
**This also is the first season since Big Brother 13 where only one Houseguest won 3 or more HoH's ([[Jackson Michie|Jackson]]).
*This is the first season since [[Big Brother 15]] where only one Houseguest won 3 PoV's or more ([[Jackson Michie|Jackson]]).
* This was the final season to feature hometown/family segments until ''[[Big Brother: Unlocked]]'' during ''[[Big Brother 27 (US)]]''.

